{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C header file", "description": "This header file defines the interface for the Configuration Service Provider (CSP) in the web server/client components. It includes function pointer typedefs for configuration operations such as adding/deleting daemons, setting modes, enabling persistent connections, and setting product names. The file also establishes a class-like structure (WEB_CSP_INTERFACE) that encapsulates these function pointers, simulating an object-oriented interface in C. It includes an external framework interface (ansc_ifo_csp.h) and contains constants for interface identification.", "external_files": ["ansc_ifo_csp.h"], "external_methods": ["ANSC_STATUS", "ACCESS_CONTAINER"], "published": ["WEB_CSP_INTERFACE_NAME", "WEB_CSP_INTERFACE_ID", "WEB_CSP_INTERFACE"], "classes": [], "methods": [{"name": "AddHttpDaemon", "description": "Function pointer to add an HTTP daemon instance to the configuration service provider."}, {"name": "DelHttpDaemon", "description": "Function pointer to delete an HTTP daemon instance based on a port."}, {"name": "SetHttpServerMode", "description": "Function pointer to set the operational mode of the HTTP server."}, {"name": "SetPersistentConn", "description": "Function pointer to enable or disable persistent HTTP connections."}, {"name": "SetProductName", "description": "Function pointer to set the product name for identification."}], "calls": ["ANSC_STATUS", "ACCESS_CONTAINER"], "search-terms": ["webConfigurationServiceProviderIf", "CSP", "web_ifo_csp.h", "configuration interface", "HTTP daemon management", "web server mode", "persistent connections", "product name setting"], "state": 2, "file_id": 8772, "knowledge_revision": 35428, "git_revision": "7e30f88c4ca54db6e79d70eb5e919c86fb3e3bcf", "ctags": [{"_type": "tag", "name": "ACCESS_WEB_CSP_INTERFACE", "path": "/home/kavia/workspace/code-generation/kirkstone-7931/rdkb/components/opensource/ccsp/CcspCommonLibrary/source/util_api/web/include/web